DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Free\, registration r
 equired\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nIn the short documentary
 \, Sueños De Una Monarca (Dreams of a Monarch)\, Director Julián Trejo B
 ax follows environmental activist Claudia Galeno-Sánchez as she turns her
  Chicago home into a monarch butterfly sanctuary and symbol of hope. After
  the showing\, Julian and Claudia will speak on a facilitated panel about 
 the significance of this project and of the monarch butterfly to many Mexi
 can-Americans in the Chicago area. Pre-registration is required for this f
 ree event.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/communit
 y-engagement-programming/suenos-de-una-monarca-documentary-showing
